# Emergency Reprint Request for Orientation Pamphlets

## Author
François Dubois

## Date
March 31, 2026

## Context
The logistics team has identified a critical issue with the orientation pamphlets intended for distribution at the upcoming orientation day. A misprint was discovered in the shipment received on March 31, 2026, rendering the pamphlets unsuitable for use. As orientation day is imminent, an emergency reprint of 200 corrected copies is requested to ensure adequate distribution to incoming students.

## Issue Summary

- **Misprint Details:**
  - Incorrect QR code linking to campus maps.
  - Typographical errors in several sections, including:
    - "Welcome Message" (Dean’s name misspelled as "Francois Duboi" instead of "François Dubois").
    - "Schedule Overview" missing a key time slot for the Dean’s opening lecture.
  - Orientation day date listed incorrectly as "April 7, 2025" instead of "April 7, 2026".

- **Impact:**
  - Risk of confusion for new students attempting to navigate the campus.
  - Potential reputational damage due to errors in printed materials.
  - Disruption to the planned schedule due to missing time slots.

## Reprint Specifications

- **Number of Copies:** 200
- **Delivery Deadline:** April 5, 2026 (2 days before orientation day)
- **Printing Requirements:**
  - High-quality glossy finish.
  - A5 size pamphlets.
  - Updated and verified QR code linking to campus maps.
  - Corrected text and schedule details.

## Corrective Actions Taken

- The communications team has updated the pamphlet content:
  - Verified Dean’s name spelling.
  - Added missing schedule time slots.
  - Corrected orientation day date.
  - Generated a new QR code for campus maps.

- Logistics team has liaised with the printing vendor to prioritize the reprint.
- Communications team is conducting a final quality assurance review of the updated content.

## Cost Estimate

- **Printing Cost per Copy:** $1.50
- **Total Cost:** $300
- **Rush Fee:** $50
- **Total Estimate:** $350

## Approval Request

**To:** Head of Logistics (Jane Smith)  
**From:** François Dubois  
**Subject:** Emergency Pamphlet Reprint Approval  

Please review and approve the emergency reprint request for 200 corrected orientation pamphlets. Timely approval will ensure the materials are delivered before orientation day, minimizing disruption.

